# .graphifyignore — what `graphify` must not index. Same pattern syntax as
# .gitignore, and it is read IN ADDITION to .gitignore. The tool's role and the
# build live in scripts/devops/build-graphify.sh.
#
# Add here only what is TRACKED but must not become graph nodes. Why gitignored
# files (including the real .env files) stay out is explained once, in the header
# of scripts/devops/build-graphify.sh, section "WHY .env STAYS OUT".
#
# The build's coverage audit reads this file too (git ls-files --exclude-from), so an
# entry here is also removed from the set of files the graph is expected to cover.

# Generated design-system bundles (two copies of one `_ds_bundle.js`, plus the
# mockup HTML/JS beside them). Measured 2026-10-22: ~4300 of the graph's ~21800
# nodes (20%) and 96% of all JavaScript nodes came from this directory. It is
# throwaway design-tool output, not code anyone navigates, and it visibly
# polluted query results. Nothing under apps/** imports from it.
docs/design/assets/
